{"version":"ai-mcq-bank-v2-la-batch15-high-quality-rewritten-affected-2026-05-22-stem-fixed-inequality-rendering-fixed-student-facing-qc-2026-05-31-pt-foundations-2026-06-11-pt-batch2-foundations-counting-2026-06-11-pt-batch3-counting-probability-rules-2026-06-11-pt-batch4-conditioning-2026-06-11-pt-batch5-random-variables-2026-06-11-pt-batch6-discrete-distributions-2026-06-11-pt-batch7-distribution-foundations-2026-06-11-pt-batch8-continuous-expectation-2026-06-11-pt-batch9-non-week7-expectation-transform-2026-06-11-pt-batch10-non-week7-process-summary-2026-06-11-pt-batch11-non-week7-final-summary-shape-2026-06-11-quality-round1-2026-06-14-quality-round2-2026-06-14-quality-round3-2026-06-14-quality-round4-deep-2026-06-14+quality-round5-difficulty-2026-06-14+quality-round6-expression-2026-06-14+quality-round7-answer-cue-2026-06-14+quality-round8-answer-shape-2026-06-14+quality-round9-answer-position-2026-06-14+quality-round10-template-padding-2026-06-14+quality-round11-generic-stems-2026-06-14+quality-round12-deterministic-cleanup-2026-06-15+quality-pilot-deep-rework-2026-06-15","concept_id":"Year-1/1a-Math-I-Calculus/composition-of-functions.html","concept":{"concept_id":"Year-1/1a-Math-I-Calculus/composition-of-functions.html","questions":[{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_composition_of_functions_e5a028fe_001","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"For functions $f\\colon X\\to Y$ and $g\\colon Y\\to Z$, how is $g\\circ f$ defined?","options":["$(g\\circ f)(x) = f(g(x))$","$(g\\circ f)(x) = f(x)+g(x)$","$(g\\circ f)(x) = g(f(x))$","$(g\\circ f)(x) = x$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"498cf0d457ccc42fac42a5ea"},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_composition_of_functions_e5a028fe_002","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"What is the interpretation of composition of functions?","options":["Two functions must have identical graphs.","One function's output becomes another's input","A function loses its domain.","A set is replaced by its complement."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"123a489cb083459b50c3fb21"},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_composition_of_functions_e5a028fe_003","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"If $f(x) = x^2$ and $g(y) = \\sin y$, what is $(g\\circ f)(x)$?","options":["$(\\sin x)^2$","$x^2+\\sin x$","$\\sin(x^2)$","$\\sin y^2$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"17620cc9e7d7d8005e61a49f"},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_composition_of_functions_e5a028fe_004","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"If $f(x) = x+1$ and $g(y) = 2y$, what is $(g\\circ f)(x)$?","options":["$2(x+1)$","$2x+1$","$x+3$","$x+1$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"b708bb07a1c5577fb4e5b9e0"},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_composition_of_functions_e5a028fe_005","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"When is the composition $g\\circ f$ defined?","options":["Whenever $f$ and $g$ have the same name.","Only when $X = Z$.","When the codomain of $f$ matches the domain of $g$","Only when both functions are constant."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"7c02d10c980f2a127dbce11e"},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_composition_of_functions_e5a028fe_006","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"If $f\\colon X\\to Y$ and $g\\colon Y\\to Z$, what is the domain and codomain of $g\\circ f$?","options":["$g\\circ f\\colon Y\\to X$","$g\\circ f\\colon Z\\to X$","$g\\circ f\\colon X\\to Z$","$g\\circ f\\colon X\\to Y$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"2c8a5dcdb561df9231b13dd6"},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_composition_of_functions_e5a028fe_007","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"Let $f\\colon X\\to Y$ and $g\\colon Y\\to Z$. Which composition is guaranteed by these sets to be defined?","options":["$f\\circ g$","$g\\circ f$","$f\\circ f$ only","$g\\circ g$ only"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"9ce0d8ea9284f28643a00a20"},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_composition_of_functions_e5a028fe_008","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"If $f(x) = x+2$ and $g(y) = y^2$, what is $(g\\circ f)(x)$?","options":["$x^2+2$","$(x+2)^2$","$x+4$","$2x^2$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"b27ef8d542ec08b4ee663d14"},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_composition_of_functions_e5a028fe_009","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"conceptual","question":"In the composition $g\\circ f$, which function is applied first?","options":["$g$ is applied first, then $f$.","$f$ is applied first, then $g$.","Both functions are applied at the same time and added.","The order is irrelevant by definition."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"7386ed6a2324c80a792616d3"},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_composition_of_functions_e5a028fe_010","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Which missing assumption can prevent $g\\circ f$ from being defined?","options":["The codomain of $f$ may fail to match the domain of $g$.","The names $f$ and $g$ may be too short.","The set $X$ may contain more than one element.","The formula for $f$ may contain $x$."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"3ebd740ab87772e62ded050e"},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_composition_of_functions_e5a028fe_011","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"application","question":"Let $f\\colon\\mathbb{R}\\to\\mathbb{R}$, $f(x) = x^2$, and $g\\colon\\mathbb{R}\\to\\mathbb{R}$, $g(y) = y+1$. What is $(g\\circ f)(2)$?","options":["$9$","$5$","$3$","$4$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"b70ab56e973f0416e8bd8ae6"},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_composition_of_functions_e5a028fe_012","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"application","question":"Suppose $f\\colon X\\to Y$ and $g\\colon W\\to Z$ with $Y\\neq W$. Is $g\\circ f$ defined?","options":["The composition $g\\circ f$ is not defined","The composition $g\\circ f$ is always defined anyway.","The composition equals $f\\circ g$ automatically.","The composition has codomain $X$."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"e8ddba47e7c919655f5f49dd"},{"id":"expansion_010_composition_of_functions_001","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Is composition commutative, that is, does $g\\circ f=f\\circ g$ in general?","options":["No; usually $g\\circ f\\ne f\\circ g$","Yes, always","Only if $f=g$","Yes, for linear functions only"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"3b34d73ee2d1d440eb3a69ae"},{"id":"expansion_010_composition_of_functions_002","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Composition of functions is associative, meaning:","options":["$(h\\circ g)\\circ f=h\\circ(g\\circ f)$","$g\\circ f=f\\circ g$","$f\\circ f=f$","$g\\circ f=g+f$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"1ffd028b4ba8cf80dcad523f"},{"id":"expansion_010_composition_of_functions_003","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"For $f\\colon X\\to Y$, what is $f\\circ \\mathrm{id}_X$?","options":["$f$","$\\mathrm{id}_X$","$\\mathrm{id}_Y$","a constant function"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"b527502edf5a350ffcf4e472"},{"id":"expansion_010_composition_of_functions_004","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"application","question":"If $f$ and $g$ are bijections, what is $(g\\circ f)^{-1}$?","options":["$f^{-1}\\circ g^{-1}$","$g^{-1}\\circ f^{-1}$","$f\\circ g$","$g\\circ f$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"b91a5144d0d72a91d213e9df"},{"id":"expansion_010_composition_of_functions_005","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"If $f(x)=x^2+1$ and $g(y)=\\sqrt y$, what is $(g\\circ f)(x)$?","options":["$\\sqrt{x^2+1}$","$x^2+\\sqrt1$","$(\\sqrt x)^2+1$","$x^2+1+\\sqrt y$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"9d699d3d2f0a16afe3feffd8"},{"id":"expansion_010_composition_of_functions_006","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"If $f(x)=x+1$ and $g(y)=2y$, what is $(f\\circ g)(x)$?","options":["$2x+2$","$x+3$","$2x+1$","$2x$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"864db111ab446752baf8bebd"},{"id":"expansion_010_composition_of_functions_007","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Which properties can composition preserve under suitable conditions?","options":["Only set complementation","Continuity and differentiability","Only cardinality","Only boundedness of finite sets"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"45efffecd57b805222e0fca8"},{"id":"expansion_010_composition_of_functions_008","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"If $f\\colon X\\to Y$, $g\\colon Y\\to Z$, and $h\\colon Z\\to W$, what is the codomain of $h\\circ(g\\circ f)$?","options":["$X$","$Y$","$W$","$Z$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"1f320699dccc60327c62fc0b"}]}}